## 🛠️ 5. Visualizing the Compilation Step

Before the Graph executes, it is "compiled" into a runtime runnable.

```javascript
import { StateGraph } from "@langchain/langgraph";

// 1. Define the structural perimeter of your application
const workflowGraph = new StateGraph(MyCustomStateDefinition)
  .addNode("generator", generateDraft)
  .addNode("evaluator", evaluateDraft)
  
  // 2. Define the Transitions
  .addEdge("__start__", "generator")
  .addConditionalEdges("generator", (state) => {
     if (state.score > 8) return "__end__"; 
     else return "evaluator";
  })
  .addEdge("evaluator", "generator"); // The Loop

// 3. Compilation prepares the optimized executable tree
const runnableApp = workflowGraph.compile();

// 4. Invocation runs the engine
const finalState = await runnableApp.invoke({ input_text: "Draft an essay on AI" });
```

